  "english": "12. Wednesday. Tone 4 [Dkh / DZ]. Fast. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 8 [dky]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God of our fathers, praised [and glorified].\"\n16. Sunday. Tone 5 [Bdz / BZ]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 5 [gy]: \"Who from eternity.\" Resurrection Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 5 [by]: \"Today [the heavenly hosts] rejoiced.\"\n22. Saturday. Tone 1 [Adz / AZ]. The Holy Patriarchs Basil of Caesarea, and the others.\n23. Sunday. Tone 2 [Aky / AK]. Fifth [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 6 [gky]: \"The pre-eternal Son.\" Resurrection Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 2 [aky]: \"Wondrous\" and \"Miraculous.\"\n24. Monday. Tone 5 [Bdz / BZ]. David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n29. Saturday. Tone 8 [Dky / DK]. James and John.\n—Eve of the Fast of the Nativity.\n30. Sunday. Tone 1 [Adz / AZ]. Sixth [Sunday]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Resurrection Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 1 [adz]: \"Awesome vision,\" to the end.\n31. Monday. Tone 2 [Aky / AK]. Canticle of the Fathers of the Fast [Harts aghts], Tone 8 [dky]: \"God of our fathers, praised.\" Say the order of the fasts.\n\nIn January:\n1. Wednesday. Tone 6 [Bdzy / BDZ]. Fast. Canticle of the Fathers of Penitence [Harts apsh], Tone 1 [adz]: \"The children sang.\"\n5. Saturday. Tone 5 [Gdz / GZ]. Eve [Candlemas] of the Nativity of Christ our God.\n11. Sunday. Tone 8 [Dky / DK]. Ninth [Sunday]. Resurrection Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 8 [dky]: \"Of the Angels,\" to the end.\n18. Sunday. Tone 7 [Ddzy / DDZ]. Tenth [Sunday]. Eve of the Fast of the Fifty Days [Yisnakats]. Resurrection Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 5 [gy]: \"Who art above,\" to the end.\n19. Monday. Tone 8 [Dky / DK]. Fast of the Fifty Days [Yisnakats]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 7 [dz]: \"Truly.\"\n21. Wednesday. Tone 2 [Aky / AK]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God, Three Years Old.\n25. Sunday. Tone 6 [Gky / GK]. First [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 5 [by]: \"Who art King.\" Resurrection Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 6 [gky]: \"Thy resurrection\" and \"Taking.\"\n26. Monday. Tone 7 [Ddzy / DDZ]. Julian and Vasilissa. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 5 [gy]: \"Those who hope in thy holy name.\"\n\nDecember\n2. Sunday. Tone 5 [Gdz / GZ]. Second [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 6 [bky]: \"Who the servant.\" Resurrection Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 5 [gy]: \"Glorified is thy [resurrection].\"\n3. Monday. Tone 6 [Gky / GK]. Genarius and Mercurius, and Yakovkos [James] and Iravophar.\n4. Tuesday. Tone 7 [Ddzy / DDZ]. King Abgar.\n9. Sunday. Tone 4 [Bky / BK]. Third [Sunday]. Eve of Saint James [Surb Hakob]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n\nTHE ROMAN SEVEN-DAY CYCLE 7.\nIn January:\n6. FRIDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ our God. The period of eating meat [non-fasting days] is ten days.\n13. Friday. Eighth day of the Nativity, and the Circumcision of Christ.\n14. Saturday. John the Forerunner [the Baptist].\n15. Sunday. Eve of the Fast of the Catechumens [Arachavor]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 7 [dz]: \"Dawn of the Only-begotten.\"\n22. Sunday. [Feast of] Saint Sarkis. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 7 [dz]: \"In glorifying.\" And for the rest, see the First Volume up to Vardavar, keeping the order of this place.\n\nFebruary:\n5. Sunday. Tone 8 [Dky / DK]. Real Eve of Great Lent [Bun Barekendan].\n14. Tuesday. Tone 1 [Adz / AZ]. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj]. See according to the order in the First Volume.",
